/E (The narrative gradually connects the present with an earlier loss. An old photograph, a warning in a notebook and a phone call using the protagonist's own voice create uncertainty about what is real. The film deliberately avoids confirming whether the protagonist is communicating with a memory, experiencing a psychological perception, encountering another version of himself, or experiencing something supernatural. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
