/P 146 0 R
/T (A major challenge in producing a psychological mystery with one actor is creating the sense of another presence without showing another performer. The solution is to use eye direction, pauses, framing and the empty space beside the protagonist. )
/E (A major challenge in producing a psychological mystery with one actor is creating the sense of another presence without showing another performer. The solution is to use eye direction, pauses, framing and the empty space beside the protagonist. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 146 0 R
/T (Another challenge is maintaining mystery within a very short duration. Too much explanation would reduce ambiguity, while too little information could make the sequence difficult to follow. The story therefore uses a small number of concrete clues: the message, photograph, notebook and voice. )
/E (Another challenge is maintaining mystery within a very short duration. Too much explanation would reduce ambiguity, while too little information could make the sequence difficult to follow. The story therefore uses a small number of concrete clues: the message, photograph, notebook and voice. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 146 0 R
/T (The final voice creates an additional production challenge because it must sound like the protagonist's voice while remaining clearly separate as an audio event. The recording and editing process must therefore preserve intelligibility without making the effect overly artificial. )
/E (The final voice creates an additional production challenge because it must sound like the protagonist's voice while remaining clearly separate as an audio event. The recording and editing process must therefore preserve intelligibility without making the effect overly artificial. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
