588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (The project provides practical learning in screenplay development, scene planning, acting, cinematography, sound design, editing and production organization. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (A significant learning outcome is understanding how a story can communicate information through visual details rather than dialogue. The photograph, notebook and empty bench each provide narrative information without requiring another on-screen character. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (The project also demonstrates the importance of restraint. Silence, a facial reaction or a repeated camera composition can be more appropriate for a psychological mystery than an elaborate visual effect. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (Working with one actor and two locations also develops practical production planning. The limited setup requires careful use of available space and encourages attention to framing, continuity and performance. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (The project further demonstrates how sound can create uncertainty. Reusing the protagonist's own voice as the mysterious caller changes the audience's understanding without requiring an additional visible character. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
