596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The expected outcome is a completed approximately three-minute psychological mystery short film titled The Empty Bench. The film is intended to engage the audience through a gradual shift from an apparently ordinary meeting to uncertainty about memory, identity and reality. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The final product should demonstrate how a minimal cast and limited locations can support an effective narrative when the visual composition, sound and editing are carefully planned. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
598 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The audience is expected to recognize the central emotional idea: sometimes letting go is harder than losing someone. However, the film should not force a single interpretation of the events. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
599 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The ending is successful for the project's purpose when it leaves the audience with the central question rather than resolving the mystery through a conventional explanation. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
