603 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The film can be developed further without changing its central concept. Future versions could refine the screenplay timing, improve continuity between the two garden scenes and conduct controlled audience screenings to study how viewers interpret the ending. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
604 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (If additional post-production resources are available, the soundscape can be refined while maintaining the film's restrained approach. The voice effect can also be adjusted to preserve the idea that the caller is the protagonist's own voice. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
605 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (A future academic extension could include a structured audience-evaluation form measuring whether viewers identify the intended themes of loss, memory, attachment and reality versus perception. Such results are not part of the current supplied project information and should be added only after actual evaluation. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
606 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The story could also be adapted into an audio-only format in future work, but the present project remains a short film and does not assume a completed podcast production. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
